A||||7||FieroHarry||Fiero VS Ferrari 308?||||12||
Z||000000||FieroHarry||06-04-2001||08:19 AM||||OKay so maybe it wasnt quite a race,<BR>Im tooling up I64 into Richmond last night on my way back to Bethesda for the last time(thank god) and flying along at 80-85MPH with two other cars (non-Fieros).<BR>Coming up onto the I-95 exit ramp I zoom up into a black car with 4 round taillights.<BR>So im thinking okay what is it?<BR>Looks like a kit but couldnt tell for sure, the exhuast pipes coming thru the vent pan in the rear were a little smaller than fieros with no trumpets.<BR>What confused me was the fact that you could see the rear struts.....<BR>I dont ever remember seeing the rear struts on any Fieros underway and am not sure whether you would be able to see them on a 308 kit or not.<P>Well to make this long story short, this off ramp breaks off to the right asnd expands over into another lane to the right. After following for 45 secs or so I broke off into the right lane and pulled along side.<BR>Gave the infamous salute (Roadhouse) and pulled away very quickly.<BR>Thic guy either didnt want to play or had no want to make any time going down the road.<BR>Within seconds he was gone from sight.<BR>Within 2 exits I stopped and got gas, jumped back on the Interstate and never saw him again.<BR>Not really a race.<BR>Roger, what do you think was it a kit?<BR>What ever it was it was black and had a third brake light, but definetly a 308<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||12
Z||000001||Wade87GT||06-04-2001||11:12 AM||||Just a bit of info, third brakelights weren't factory installed on the 308 and they don't have struts (suspension) either. <A HREF="http://home.att.net/~ferrari/308faq1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.att.net/~ferrari/308faq1.htm</A> <P>Wade<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||06-04-2001||02:33 PM||||what Wade said Harry. And you know what, now that you mentioned it I just got out my Ferrari bible. Not one of the Ferraris in there has 3rd brake lite that I can find. Wonder how DOT let them get away with that..I thought all US sold cars were required to have it. My book goes clear up to 90's models.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodney||06-04-2001||04:29 PM||||308's were made from 1976-85. The USA third brake light requirement started in 86. All 328's and up have them. Just like the 86 and up Fiero's.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||06-04-2001||04:41 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rodney:<BR><B>308's were made from 1976-85. The USA third brake light requirement started in 86. All 328's and up have them. Just like the 86 and up Fiero's.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I wonder why my book shows no brake lite on any 328, 348, testa rossa, 355. maybe they were dealer installed?<P>also more on Ferrari lites while were on the subject. Only the US cars had the back up lites in the center of rear tail lite lens. Euro models were like fog lites, mounted under the rear bumper.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
